Carafe: the Horizon server keeps low-level keyboard and mouse hooks (WH_KEYBOARD_LL, WH_MOUSE_LL). They are global,
run in the thread that set them, and every key, mouse move, button and wheel turn from the controller also goes to
that thread as a low-level hook message, without waiting for the hook's answer, which is taken and dropped. A thread
that has ended gets none, and one that does not read its messages keeps at most 64. The mouse hook is told the
movement from where the cursor is when the hook takes the message, so DirectInput 7 and older, which reads the mouse
and keyboard through these hooks, sees the movement. Journal and win event hooks are still refused.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

